          "integer": true,
          "kind": "number",
          "max": 168,
          "min": 2,
          "name": "every_hours",
          "required": false,
        },
        {
          "description": "Weekdays for repeat 'weekly', e.g. ['mon','thu'] for "Mondays and Thursdays". Defaults to today's weekday in time_zone; omit for any other repeat.",
          "itemKind": "enum",
          "kind": "array",
          "name": "days",
          "required": false,
          "values": [
            "mon",
            "tue",
            "wed",
            "thu",
            "fri",
            "sat",
            "sun",
          ],
        },
        {
          "description": "Local hours a job may run in, 'HH:MM-HH:MM', e.g. '22:00-08:00' for "at night"; '22:00-06:00' crosses midnight. Each run then picks its cleanest hour inside that day's window. Only with repeat 'daily', 'weekdays' or 'weekly'; omit to allow any hour.",
          "kind": "string",
          "name": "window",
          "required": false,
        },
        {
          "description": "IANA zone that window and days are read in, e.g. 'Europe/Berlin'; take it from the user's location. Defaults to the host's system zone. Only with a job repeat.",
          "kind": "string",
          "name": "time_zone",
          "required": false,
        },
        {
          "description": "Claude Code session id of the conversation that queued the task. Omit it: the server finds the current session itself when the Tidegap plugin is installed. Pass it only when the host substitutes it (e.g. \${CLAUDE_SESSION_ID} in a slash command); it then wins. Values that are not 8-128 letters, digits, '-' or '_' are ignored.",
          "kind": "string",
          "name": "origin_session_id",
          "required": false,
        },
        {
          "description": "true when the user says "after my limit resets": the task starts no earlier than the Claude subscription limit reset (the latest reset of an exhausted 5-hour or weekly window, else the fuller window's reset; see tidegap_usage), then runs at the cleanest hour after it. The deadline rises to at least two hours after the reset. Fails, queuing nothing, when no limit reading exists. Defaults to false; cannot combine with not_before.",
          "kind": "boolean",
          "name": "after_limit_reset",
          "required": false,
        },
        {
          "description": "Earliest start, ISO-8601 with offset, e.g. '2026-05-12T18:00:00+02:00' for "not before 6pm" or "after lunch". The task then runs at the cleanest hour between it and the deadline; it must be in the future and not after the deadline. Omit to allow any time up to the deadline; cannot combine with after_limit_reset.",
          "format": "date-time",
          "kind": "string",
          "name": "not_before",
          "required": false,
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "annotations": {
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false,
        "readOnlyHint": false,
        "title": "Show task queue",
      },
      "description": "Show the local task queue and jobs: every task in brief or one in full. Use when: the user asks what is queued or repeats, whether a task finished, or for its result. Do not use to change a task (use cancel_task, postpone_task, update_deadline or retry_task) or for limits (use tidegap_usage). Behavior: no network or login; marks a shown completed or failed task read; never changes a status. Returns: without task_id, status counts, last_tick_at, a line per task and job (guarantee, next run and id, last result); with task_id, its prompt, result, receipt and events. Rejects an unknown task_id.",
      "name": "check_queue_status",
      "params": [
        {
          "description": "One task's id, e.g. 't-3f2a…', from schedule_task or this tool's summary, to get its full record. Omit for the summary of all tasks.",
          "kind": "string",
