        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "annotations": {
        "destructiveHint": true,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false,
        "readOnlyHint": false,
        "title": "Cancel one task",
      },
      "description": "Cancel one queued or scheduled task by task_id; for all pending, use cancel_all. Use when: the user drops one task. Do not use to delay it (use postpone_task) or rerun a failed one (use retry_task). Behavior: marks it cancelled locally (no network) and redacts its prompt. Also cancels running and submitted tasks; a Batch call may still bill. A job or series skips this run; series=true ends it, even from a finished run. Else a finished task or repeat call changes nothing. Returns: "Task <id> status: <status>", terminated_at, and a job or series line when ended. Rejects an unknown task_id.",
      "name": "cancel_task",
      "params": [
        {
          "description": "Id of the task to cancel, e.g. 't-3f2a…', from the schedule_task reply or the check_queue_status list.",
          "kind": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "name": "task_id",
          "required": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "true also ends the job or series this task is a run of, so no further run is queued; use it for "stop this for good". Defaults to false: skip only this run; a job then plans its next one. No effect on a one-off task.",
          "kind": "boolean",
          "name": "series",
          "required": false,
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "annotations": {
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": false,
        "openWorldHint": true,
        "readOnlyHint": false,
        "title": "Run task now",
      },
      "description": "Run one queued or scheduled task now, skipping its clean window. Use when: the user wants the result now. Do not use for a failed task (use retry_task), to pick a new deadline (use update_deadline), or for a claude-code task (run \`tidegap queue run-now <id>\`). Behavior: drops its earliest start and makes one provider call at the current grid intensity; needs the task provider's key in the server env (and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY); the receipt records intensitySource=expedited. Returns: status and error on failure. Rejects running, submitted, finished and unknown tasks.",
      "name": "expedite_task",
      "params": [
        {
          "description": "Id of the queued or scheduled task to run now, e.g. 't-3f2a…', from the schedule_task reply or the check_queue_status list.",
          "kind": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "name": "task_id",
          "required": true,
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "annotations": {
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": true,
