      "description": "Run a failed task again now, with the same prompt, provider and model. Use when: a task failed on a transient error (rate limit, 5xx) and the user wants it redone. Do not use for a task that did not fail (use expedite_task to run it now, update_deadline to move it). Behavior: one provider call now, through the OpenClaw runtime or a provider key in the plugin config; the new result and signed receipt replace the old ones, then the result is delivered. Returns: status, error on failure, result, receipt and delivery. Throws on tasks that are not failed and unknown task_ids.",
      "name": "retry_task",
      "params": [
        {
          "description": "Id of the failed task to run again, e.g. 't-3f2a…', from the check_queue_status list (status failed).",
          "kind": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "name": "task_id",
          "required": true,
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "annotations": {
        "destructiveHint": true,
        "idempotentHint": false,
        "openWorldHint": false,
        "readOnlyHint": false,
        "title": "Cancel all pending tasks",
      },
      "description": "Cancel every queued and scheduled task in the local queue at once; for a single task use cancel_task. Use when: the user says "cancel everything" or "clear the queue". Do not use to drop one task or to end a repeating series (use cancel_task, with series=true for a series). Behavior: marks each pending task cancelled; running, submitted and finished tasks stay as they are; no network or login. A repeating task skips this occurrence and its next one is queued, so a second call cancels that one too. Returns: matched, cancelled, and errors (task_id and error per task that could not be cancelled).",
      "name": "cancel_all",
      "params": [
        {
          "description": "Cancel only tasks in one state: 'queued' (no window picked yet) or 'scheduled' (window picked). Omit to cancel both.",
          "kind": "enum",
          "name": "status",
          "required": false,
          "values": [
            "queued",
            "scheduled",
          ],
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "description": "Set how a scheduled task's result is delivered when it completes; several modes allowed. Use when: right after schedule_task, once the user has chosen. Do not use to read a result (use check_queue_status). Behavior: saves the setting locally, without checking the task exists; sends nothing now. queue transmits nothing; chat may route through Telegram; telegram, webhook and file send or write the FULL result, so confirm those destinations first. Default: chat. Returns: task_id and the saved delivery. Throws on a missing webhook_url or file_path.",
      "name": "set_delivery",
      "params": [
        {
          "description": "Id of the task, e.g. 't-3f2a…', from the schedule_task reply or the check_queue_status list.",
          "kind": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "name": "task_id",
          "required": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "The modes the user chose, e.g. ['telegram'] or ['chat','file']. webhook needs webhook_url; file needs file_path. Confirm telegram, webhook and file destinations with the user first.",
          "itemKind": "enum",
          "kind": "array",
          "name": "deliver",
          "required": true,
          "values": [
            "chat",
            "telegram",
            "webhook",
            "file",
            "queue",
            "os",
          ],
        },
        {
          "description": "URL that receives the full result as a POST, e.g. 'https://example.com/hooks/tidegap'. Needed when deliver includes 'webhook'; omit otherwise.",
          "kind": "string",
          "name": "webhook_url",
          "required": false,
        },
        {
          "description": "Path on the gateway host to write the report to, e.g. '/var/reports/digest.md'. Needed when deliver includes 'file'; omit otherwise.",
          "kind": "string",
          "name": "file_path",
          "required": false,
        },
        {
          "description": "Report format for 'file' delivery, e.g. 'html'. Default: md. 'pdf' renders the HTML report and needs puppeteer on the gateway.",
          "kind": "enum",
          "name": "file_format",
          "required": false,
          "values": [
            "md",
            "html",
            "txt",
            "json",
            "pdf",
          ],
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
}
`;
